Q: Delete line if substitution would leave it empty A: <p>You can look if the line contains &quot;foo&quot;, if it does, remove all the &quot;foo&quot;s, and if what remains is not blank, print it.</p>
<pre class="lang-perl prettyprint-override"><code>#!/usr/bin/env perl
use strict;
use warnings;

while (&lt;DATA&gt;) {
    if (/foo/) {
        s/foo//g; 
        next if m/^\s*$/;
    }
    print;
}

__DATA__
foo foo foo
foo bar

bar bar
foo bar bar
foo
</code></pre>
<p>prints:</p>
<pre><code> bar

bar bar
 bar bar
</code></pre>
<p>Change to <code>s/\s*foo\s*//g;</code> to also remove spaces around the &quot;foo&quot;s and print</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>bar

bar bar
bar bar
</code></pre>
